Don't reference render_is_threaded_video() when building the libretro
shared library — that symbol lives in render_sdl.c which is excluded
from the libretro build, so the resulting .so loads with an unresolved
symbol that the dynamic linker reports at first use:

    symbol lookup error: undefined symbol: render_is_threaded_video

The libretro path is single-threaded anyway (the threaded video path
is already guarded out in 003-fix-vdp-nothread.patch); just skip the
branch under IS_LIB so libdl never has to find the symbol.
--- a/vdp.c
+++ b/vdp.c
@@ -511,9 +511,11 @@ vdp_context *init_vdp_context(uint8_t region_pal, uint8_t has_max_vsram, uint8_t
 {
 	vdp_context *context;
 #ifndef _WIN32
+#ifndef IS_LIB
 	if (render_is_threaded_video()) {
 		context = ret->renderer = init_vdp_context_int(region_pal, has_max_vsram, type);
 	} else
+#endif
 #endif
 	{
